<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Madagascar</h1><p class="st-meta">1960 CE – present · capital Antananarivo</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An island republic in the Indian Ocean, independent from France since 26 June 1960, with four republics and repeated political crises since.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-madagascar">French Madagascar</a> became the autonomous Malagasy Republic within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-community">French Community</a> on 14 October 1958, after the Malagasy Uprising of 1947 and the Loi Cadre reforms of 1956. A constitution followed in 1959, and full independence came on 26 June 1960 under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philibert-tsiranana">Philibert Tsiranana</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The First Republic (1960–72) kept strong ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> until protests overturned Tsiranana in 1972. Military rulers followed, and Didier Ratsiraka's Marxist–Leninist Second Republic ran from 1975 to 1993. The economy collapsed and the country was bankrupt by 1979. After protests in 1991 a transitional government led by Albert Zafy began the Third Republic, a multi-party democracy. Marc Ravalomanana won a contested 2001 election. In 2009 Andry Rajoelina pushed him from power, a change widely condemned as a coup d'état, and a new constitution in 2010 established a Fourth Republic.</p><h2>To the present</h2><p>Rajoelina won the 2018 election and was re-elected in November 2023 amid an opposition boycott. Protests in 2025 ended with his flight and impeachment, and the military took control. On 17 October 2025 Colonel Michael Randrianirina was sworn in as president.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/madagascar.jpg" alt="Madagascar" width="330" height="220"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Madagascar.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1960 CE – present</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Antananarivo</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philibert Tsiranana, Didier Ratsiraka, Albert Zafy, Marc Ravalomanana, Andry Rajoelina</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity, traditional faiths</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malagasy, French</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/madagascar">Madagascar</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Madagascar, Malagasy Republic</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1993&amp;focus=madagascar" aria-label="Madagascar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-globe map-loc" viewBox="0 0 10000 10000" role="img" aria-label="Globe: where Madagascar lay"><image href="/maps/globes/g060s30.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="10000"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3999 4112L3999 4112"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3999 4112h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3999 4112h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3999 4112h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Antananarivo. <a href="/atlas?year=1993&amp;focus=madagascar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
